! FCALCD.DBG: fcalc under the debugger, while it computes fact(3) with the
! user's function fact(n) = if(n < 2, 1, n * fact(n - 1)). Each call of a
! user's function is a call of FCEVAL.CALL_USER, so its break stops at each
! level of the recursion; at each, the expression trees are walked through
! their pointers (a node's KID, the first operand or argument, and its NEXT).
SET LOG FCALCD.DLG
SET OUTPUT LOG,VERIFY
SET RADIX DECIMAL
SET BREAK FCEVAL.CALL_USER
! fact(3), typed: P is the call's node, FN the function, its BODY the tree of
! if(...), a call (N_CALL, 3) whose first argument is the comparison n < 2
! (N_OPERATION, 4; OP_COMPARE + 3, 23, < being the third relation).
GO
EXAMINE FN%NAME
EXAMINE FN%COUNT
EXAMINE FN%PARAMS(1)
EXAMINE FN%BODY%KIND
EXAMINE FN%BODY%NAME
EXAMINE FN%BODY%KID%KIND
EXAMINE FN%BODY%KID%OP
EXAMINE FN%BODY%KID%KID%NAME
! The argument 3, a number (N_NUMBER, 1), and the argument after it: none.
EXAMINE P%KID%KIND
EXAMINE P%KID%NUMBER
EXAMINE P%KID%NEXT%KIND
! fact(n - 1), from the body: its argument is n - 1 (OP_SUB, 2), whose
! operands are the name n and the number 1. F is the caller's frame: n is 3.
GO
EXAMINE P%NAME
EXAMINE P%KID%OP
EXAMINE P%KID%KID%NAME
EXAMINE P%KID%KID%NEXT%NUMBER%Z
EXAMINE F%NAMES(1)
EXAMINE CALLS
! fact(n - 1) again, n 2: the stack holds three calls of CALL_USER, each
! through EVALUATE, CALL_FUNCTION, IF's CHOOSE, and OPERATE's n * ...
GO
SHOW CALLS
EXAMINE CALLS
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
GO
EXIT
